# Teaching Kit content upgrades

Canonical rules: `docs/teaching-kit/CONTENT_UPGRADE_RULES.md`

When upgrading or enriching lesson / Teaching Kit curriculum:

## Forbidden

- Redesigning, moving, renaming, or skipping Teaching Kit binder sections
- Removing existing functionality
- Generating or replacing cover images
- Generating activity images or publishing AI placeholder artwork
- Generating printable files or packs
- Copying copyrighted book text or song lyrics
- Destructive rewrites that drop legacy lesson content

## Required

- Non-destructive upgrades into the **existing** Teaching Kit structure
- Age-appropriate activities only (infants ≠ preschool; toddlers ≠ kindergarten)
- Complete educational sections (objectives, materials, prep, activities, books, songs, toolkit, family, observations, etc.)
- Printables as **Printable Needed** placeholders / ideas only
- Images as **Image Needed** briefs / prompts only (owner creates art later)
- Weak covers: flag + detailed owner image prompt — never auto-replace artwork
- Original activities inspired by current ECE best practices (not short-lived trends)
- Before marking complete: review as a provider paying $19.99/month; fix anything incomplete, repetitive, or weak

## Songs / books

- Books: title, author, brief description, discussion ideas only
- Songs: full lyrics only for original / public-domain; copyrighted songs → title + when to use (no lyrics)
